---
import LegalLayout from "@layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How LeadOrbiq handles information related to the Chrome extension and this website."
  pathname="/privacy-policy/"
  lastUpdated="August 1, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how LeadOrbiq ("we," "us," or "the extension") handles information
    in connection with the LeadOrbiq Chrome extension and this website. A few sections describe
    implementation details that are still being finalized — we've noted those clearly rather than
    guess, and this policy will be reviewed against the shipped extension before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What LeadOrbiq is</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is a Chrome extension designed to help users collect and organize business lead
    information while researching prospects, primarily through Google Maps. It is not a standalone
    web application.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information the extension may handle</h2>
  <p>
    In the course of helping you collect and organize business information from Google Maps,
    LeadOrbiq may process publicly visible business listing details (such as business name and
    category) that you choose to collect during your research. The complete, confirmed list of data
    fields the extension collects is published on the <a href="/features/">Features page</a> and kept
    in sync with this policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    Whether additional fields — such as phone numbers, websites, ratings, or email addresses — are
    collected, and the exact source of any such data, is still being finalized and will be documented
    here once confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Account and purchase information</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is offered on Monthly, Yearly, and Lifetime plans (see <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>).
    Purchasing a plan involves standard billing information handled by our payment processor. The
    exact account setup and what's stored on our side is still being finalized and will be described
    here once confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Whether collected lead data is stored locally in your browser, synced to a cloud account, or
    both, is still being finalized. This section will describe the actual storage behavior once
    confirmed against the current extension release.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
  <p>Specific data retention periods are still being finalized.</p>

  <h2>6. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Any third-party processors, analytics tools, or payment processors used in connection with
    LeadOrbiq will be listed here once confirmed. We won't claim "we never share data with third
    parties" or similar blanket statements until that claim can be technically verified.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Chrome extension permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Chrome extensions must declare the permissions they request. Review the permissions listed on
    the LeadOrbiq Chrome Web Store listing before installing. A plain-language explanation of each
    requested permission, matched to the current extension release, will be added here once
    confirmed.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <p>
    If you use LeadOrbiq to collect information about businesses for outreach purposes, you are
    responsible for using that information lawfully. This includes following applicable privacy and
    marketing laws, respecting Google Maps' and any other platform's terms of use, identifying
    yourself accurately, personalizing your outreach, avoiding spam, and honoring opt-out requests.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    LeadOrbiq is intended for business and professional use and is not directed at children. We do
    not knowingly collect personal information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data requests</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question about data handled in connection with LeadOrbiq, or want to submit a
    privacy request, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> and select "Privacy request" as the
    topic. We aim to respond promptly. A formal data-deletion request process will be documented here
    once finalized.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy as the product and its confirmed capabilities change. Material
    changes will be reflected in the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}
      >{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a
    >
    or through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
